    {
      "chord_quality": "6",
      "function_role": "color-tone-addition-policy",
      "narrative": "Roberts explicitly names the sixth as a coloristic extension that does not change a chord's scale function: \"the addition of the extensions Maj. 7th, 6th, 9th, etc., only affect the color and texture of the chord\" (chapter 4, p. 36). The 6th chord is therefore interchangeable with its triad or maj7 form for purposes of progression logic.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
