    {
      "chord_quality": "6",
      "function_role": "dominant-function-recontextualization",
      "narrative": "Roberts demonstrates that a 6th chord can carry dominant 7b9 function when read in phrase context: \"The G6 in bar 3 is functioning as a dominant chord (Eb + 7b9)\" (chapter 3, p. 12). This is a concrete instance of Roberts's principle that functional identity depends on full phrase analysis, not isolated chord spelling.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "four-voice-melodic-motion"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "chord-melody",
      "references": [
