    {
      "chord_quality": "add9",
      "function_role": "color-tone-addition-policy",
      "narrative": "Roberts names the ninth among the extensions that \"only affect the color and texture of the chord and do not change its scale function or its role in the progression\" (chapter 4, p. 36). The ninth may therefore be added to any chord freely in chord melody arranging without altering the harmonic grammar of the passage.",
