    {
      "chord_quality": "aug",
      "function_role": "chromatic-passing-chord-altered-shape",
      "narrative": "Roberts's chapter 3 passing-chord study employs m7+5 shapes (minor seventh with augmented fifth) as chromatic connective tissue between diatonic chords, demonstrating that augmented-fifth voicings belong to his palette of altered passing chords (chapter 3, p. 11). The augmented quality is treated not as a harmonic destination but as a linking texture that creates \"interesting extensions\" from the independence of melody and harmony (chapter 4, p. 40).",
      "source_principle_ids": [
