    {
      "chord_quality": "any",
      "function_role": "voice-leading-sustain-policy",
      "narrative": "Roberts states his universal chord-tone sustain rule across all chord qualities: \"Sustain each chordal tone for as long as possible. In general, this means to keep your fingers in place until it's absolutely necessary to move them. This will contribute measurably to the continuity of your chord melody style\" (chapter 3, p. 15). The rule is not quality-specific \u2014 it applies to every chord the player voices.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
