    {
      "chord_quality": "any",
      "function_role": "block-chord-voicing-change-per-melody-note",
      "narrative": "Roberts prescribes that in block chord style every melody note must be accompanied by a freshly voiced chord: \"it is more desirable to change the voicing or inversion with each new melody note, in order to create the effect of all lines moving at once\" (chapter 2, p. 9). Leaving the chord form unchanged while the melody moves \"tends to destroy the block chord effect\" \u2014 a proscriptive corollary.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "block-chord-voicing-change-per-note"
