    {
      "chord_quality": "any",
      "function_role": "block-chord-static-form-prohibition",
      "narrative": "Roberts explicitly warns against leaving the chord form unchanged when the melody moves in block chord style: \"Often the melody can be fingered easily without having to change the chord form, but this tends to destroy the block chord effect\" (chapter 2, p. 9). The student must change voicing or inversion with each new melody note even when it is mechanically unnecessary.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
