    {
      "chord_quality": "any",
      "function_role": "short-punctuation-placement-policy",
      "narrative": "Roberts prescribes that short chord punctuations must be \"played with authority and appropriately placed within the bar\" to maintain harmonic continuity without constant restriking (chapter 2, p. 10). Harmonic continuity can be further reinforced by \"choosing melodies which emphasize chordal tones\" \u2014 the melodic line does harmonic work that the sparse chord cannot do alone.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "short-punctuation-harmonic-continuity"
