    {
      "chord_quality": "any",
      "function_role": "solo-guitar-arrangement-working-method",
      "narrative": "Roberts prescribes a deliberately modest iterative method for developing chord melody arrangements: \"develop chord melody solos for each of these examples, keeping them as simple as possible. Concentrate mainly on finding chord voicings that sound good to you and still permit the melody to be played\" (chapter 4, p. 42). Simplicity is the starting constraint, not the final destination \u2014 repetition builds instinct toward extemporaneous chord melody (chapter 4, p. 52).",
